cfg179_s4_swirl_bounds  mode = main  (kappa = 1/2 FITTED; P2 nu = sqrt(1 + 1/y); footings canonical 9.3603e-11, alt 1.1312e-10 m/s^2)
G8 declared bound: co/counter contrast <= 10^0.043 - 1 = 0.1041  (gate 1.02's 95% intrinsic scatter)
SPARC sample (Q <= 2, V_flat > 0, R_d > 0, i >= 30 deg, rotmod present): N = 123 galaxies, 2858 points (g_bar with Upsilon_disk 0.5, Upsilon_bul 0.7: used only for S-a0's binning)
  [PASS] C1 CONTROL: the SPARC sample is non-trivial (>= 100 galaxies) and every galaxy has a spin proxy
         N = 123

==============================================================================================================
S-F  FRESNEL DRAG: the river dragged in proportion to the matter density
==============================================================================================================
  canonical: rho_Lambda = 8.632e-08 Msun/pc^3; rho_b = 0.08 -> lambda_c = 1 - 1.08e-06.  Prograde balance leaves gravity (1 - lambda_c) V^2/R; a retrograde tracer at speed u feels a_R = -lambda_c^2 V^2/R + (|u| + lambda_c V) lambda_c V/R - g -> net OUTWARD for every |u| (no retrograde orbit exists)
  canonical: rho_Lambda = 8.632e-08 Msun/pc^3; rho_b = 0.001 -> lambda_c = 1 - 8.63e-05.  Prograde balance leaves gravity (1 - lambda_c) V^2/R; a retrograde tracer at speed u feels a_R = -lambda_c^2 V^2/R + (|u| + lambda_c V) lambda_c V/R - g -> net OUTWARD for every |u| (no retrograde orbit exists)
  alt      : rho_Lambda = 1.261e-07 Msun/pc^3; rho_b = 0.08 -> lambda_c = 1 - 1.58e-06.  Prograde balance leaves gravity (1 - lambda_c) V^2/R; a retrograde tracer at speed u feels a_R = -lambda_c^2 V^2/R + (|u| + lambda_c V) lambda_c V/R - g -> net OUTWARD for every |u| (no retrograde orbit exists)
  alt      : rho_Lambda = 1.261e-07 Msun/pc^3; rho_b = 0.001 -> lambda_c = 1 - 1.26e-04.  Prograde balance leaves gravity (1 - lambda_c) V^2/R; a retrograde tracer at speed u feels a_R = -lambda_c^2 V^2/R + (|u| + lambda_c V) lambda_c V/R - g -> net OUTWARD for every |u| (no retrograde orbit exists)
  [PASS] S-F [HEADLINE] a Fresnel-like drag is excluded: lambda_c exceeds 0.999 wherever galaxies have stars or gas, so bound retrograde or counter-rotating orbits could not exist -- yet they do (counter-rotating discs, retrograde halo stars; standard knowledge, not a committed dataset)
         canonical|0.08: 1 - lambda_c = 1.1e-06; canonical|0.001: 1 - lambda_c = 8.6e-05; alt|0.08: 1 - lambda_c = 1.6e-06; alt|0.001: 1 - lambda_c = 1.3e-04

==============================================================================================================
S-u  UNIVERSAL DRAG and the G8 co/counter-rotation bound
==============================================================================================================
  a universal lambda_c only rescales every prograde disc's radial force by 1/(1 - lambda_c): it is absorbed into the fitted
  law (SPARC cannot see it).  Co/counter contrast 2 lambda_c (1 + s) V^2/R <= 0.1041 V^2/R at s = 0 -> lambda_c <= 0.0520 (s = +0.1: 0.0473; s = -0.1: 0.0578)

==============================================================================================================
S-j  SPIN-SCALED DRAG against the RAR's intrinsic scatter
==============================================================================================================
  j = 2 R_d V_flat: median 700 kpc km/s, 5-95%: 65 - 3453; std log10 j = 0.53 dex
  p = 1.0: lambda_max = 0.0437 (set by the RAR scatter); median galaxy lambda_c = 0.0437, most spinning 0.438, a Milky-Way disc (R_d 2.6, 220 km/s) 0.0714;  at 0.048: lambda_max 0.0477
  p = 0.5: lambda_max = 0.1264 (set by the RAR scatter); median galaxy lambda_c = 0.1264, most spinning 0.400, a Milky-Way disc (R_d 2.6, 220 km/s) 0.1616;  at 0.048: lambda_max 0.1379
  p = 2.0: lambda_max = 0.0052 (set by the RAR scatter); median galaxy lambda_c = 0.0052, most spinning 0.522, a Milky-Way disc (R_d 2.6, 220 km/s) 0.0139;  at 0.048: lambda_max 0.0056
  [PASS] S-j [HEADLINE] a drag that grows with the disc's spin (p = 1) is bounded by the RAR's tightness before it saturates: the scatter it adds reaches 0.043 dex at a median-galaxy lambda_c below the G8 bound
         lambda_max = 0.0437 (median galaxy), Milky Way 0.0714, most spinning 0.438; G8's universal bound 0.0520

